msgid "Collect performance metrics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/_static/badges/entry-ent.rst:9
msgid ""
"|plans-img-yellow| Available on `Entry, Enterprise, and Enterprise "
"Advanced plans <https://mattermost.com/pricing/>`__ (not available on "
"Professional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:6
msgid "plans-img-yellow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:7
msgid ""
"System admins can collect and store the :doc:`same performance monitoring"
" metrics </administration-guide/scale/performance-monitoring-metrics>` as"
" Prometheus, without having to deploy these third-party tools. Data is "
"collected every minute and is stored in a path you configure. The data is"
" synchronized to either a cloud-based or local file store every hour, and"
" retained for 15 days."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:9
msgid ""
"Download and share the collected data with Mattermost to understand "
"application performance, troubleshoot system stability and performance, "
"as well as inform route cause analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:13
msgid ""
"Already have Prometheus and Grafana deployed? You can :doc:`use these "
"tools to monitor performance of your Mattermost deployment "
"</administration-guide/scale/deploy-prometheus-grafana-for-performance-"
"monitoring>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:16
msgid "Mattermost configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:20
msgid ""
"For Mattermost Cloud deployments, no setup is required. See the `usage "
"<#usage>`__ section below for details on collecting performance metrics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:22
msgid ""
"For a self-hosted Mattermost deployment, a Mattermost system admin must "
"perform the following steps in Mattermost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:24
msgid ""
"Log in to your Mattermost :doc:`workspace </end-user-guide/end-user-"
"guide-index>` as a system admin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:25
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v10.1, you can install the Metrics plugin from the in-"
"product Mattermost Marketplace by selecting the **Product** |product-"
"list| icon and selecting **App Marketplace**. Search for **Metrics** and "
"select **Install**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:100
msgid ""
"Navigate between Channels, collaborative playbooks, and boards using the "
"product menu icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:26
msgid ""
"Go to **System Console > Plugins > Plugin Management**. In the "
"**Installed Plugins** section, scroll to **Mattermost Metrics Plugin**, "
"and select **Enable Plugin**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:27
msgid "Specify the path of the time-series database, and select **Save**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:28
msgid ""
"Go to **System Console > Environment > Performance Monitoring**, and set "
"**Enable Performance Monitoring** to **true**. Select **Save**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:29
msgid ""
"Go to **System Console > Environment > Performance Monitoring**, and set "
"**Enable Client Performance Monitoring** to **true**. This setting is "
"required for the system administrator's performance monitoring product "
"experience. Select **Save**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:33
msgid ""
"For Mattermost deployments prior to v10.1, you must download the latest "
"version of `the plugin binary release <https://github.com/mattermost"
"/mattermost-plugin-metrics/releases>`__, compatible with Mattermost "
"v8.0.1 and later. Go to **System Console > Plugins > Plugin Management > "
"Upload Plugin**, and upload the plugin binary you downloaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:36
msgid "Upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:38
msgid ""
"We recommend upgrading this feature as new versions are released. "
"Generally, updates are seamless and don't interrupt the user experience "
"in Mattermost. Visit the `Releases page <https://github.com/mattermost"
"/mattermost-plugin-metrics/releases>`__ for the latest release, available"
" releases, and compatibiilty considerations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:41
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:43
msgid ""
"You need to be a Mattermost system admin to collect performance metrics. "
"Select **Create Dump** to generate dump files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:45
msgid ""
"To use the generated dump file, you can simply clone the `Dockprom "
"<https://github.com/stefanprodan/dockprom>`__ repository. Change the "
"Prometheus data volume to point to the dump that you just downloaded. The"
" downloaded file is compressed, so to be able to use it, you need to "
"decompress it first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:47
msgid ""
"The volume configuration for Prometheus should look like the code below "
"in the ``docker-compose.yml`` file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:55
msgid ""
"Once you set this up, run ``docker-compose`` as described in `Dockprom "
"Repository <https://github.com/stefanprodan/dockprom?tab=readme-ov-"
"file#install>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:57
msgid ""
"You can also use our `Mattermost Performance Monitoring v2 "
"<https://grafana.com/grafana/dashboards/15582-mattermost-performance-"
"monitoring-v2/>`_ dashboard by simply importing it into Grafana."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:59
msgid "Open Grafana (``<localhost>:3000`` by default) and then log into it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:60
msgid ""
"Once you log in, go to the **Plus** |plus| icon on the left sidebar, and "
"then select **Import**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:31
msgid "The Plus icon provides access to channel and direct message functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:61
msgid ""
"Enter the dashboard ID (``15582``) in the **Grafana.com Dashboard** "
"field, and then select **Load** to fetch the dashboard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:64
msgid "What's collected?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/scale/collect-performance-metrics.rst:66
msgid ""
"Mattermost provides :ref:`custom metrics <administration-guide/scale"
"/performance-monitoring-metrics:custom Mattermost metrics>` and "
":ref:`standard Go metrics <administration-guide/scale/performance-"
"monitoring-metrics:standard go metrics>` that can be used to monitor your"
" system's performance. Additionally Enterprise customers can use the "
"Metrics plugin to collect :ref:`host/system metrics <administration-"
"guide/scale/performance-monitoring-metrics:host/system metrics>` from "
"`node exporter <https://github.com/prometheus/node_exporter>`_ targets to"
" monitor network-related panels for Mattermost Calls."
msgstr ""

